---
import { SITE_DESCRIPTION, SITE_TITLE } from "../consts";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title={SITE_TITLE}
  description={SITE_DESCRIPTION}
  className="flex min-h-svh max-w-sm flex-col justify-center"
>
  <main class="space-y-4">
    <p>Hi! I'm Héctor.</p>
    <p>
      I'm a software engineer from Spain, passionate about building backend
      systems that run quietly and unnoticed in the background (that means they
      work).
    </p>
    <p>
      At <a href="https://emailmeter.com">Email Meter</a>, I handle vast amounts
      of real-time email data daily using Python, BigQuery, Dataflow, and AI for
      automated categorization.
    </p>
    <p>
      I'm also building <a href="https://www.reportative.com">Reportative</a>,
      which turns data from software and industrial devices into dashboards.
      Right now that means insulation monitoring: small nodes on site read the
      monitoring devices over Modbus TCP and MQTT, keep their history and send
      it to the cloud, where ClickHouse crunches it and the people in charge
      see what is failing and what to do about it.
    </p>
    <p>Other <a href="/projects">projects</a>:</p>
    <ul class="list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5 marker:text-zinc-400">
      <li>
        <a href="https://md.hache.xyz">MarkShare</a>, a self-hosted Markdown
        sharing platform.
      </li>
      <li>relay, a message relay between AI agents.</li>
      <li>
        <a href="/blog/tailnet-acl-map">Tailnet ACL Map</a>, a visualizer for
        Tailscale ACLs.
      </li>
      <li>Tachikoma, a talking ESP32 companion with a face.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      I also love analog photography — feel free to explore my work in <a
        href="/gallery">/gallery</a
      >.
    </p>
    <p>🙋🏻‍♂️ 🇪🇸 ❤️ 🛠️ 🐍 ⚡ 📷</p>
  </main>
</Layout>
